  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "A parking garage initially contains $70$ vehicles. The number of vehicles in the garage $V(t)$ increases at a rate that obeys an inhibited growth model, where $t\\ge 0$ is the time in hours. If the maximum capacity of the garage is $250$ vehicles, which differential equation could be used to model the number of vehicles in the garage? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.",
